title: The Banking Clan's Price
subtitle: The Republic owes the Muuns too much, and they know it.
tags: event
view-if: debt >= 20 and banking_clan_timer <= 0 and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 2
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg
on-arrival: banking_clan_timer = 8

= The Banking Clan's Price

The Republic owes the InterGalactic Banking Clan [+ debt_txt +], and the Clan's chairman, **San Hill**, has come to Coruscant to discuss it. He is very polite. He would like the Republic to be polite in return.

*The more the Republic owes, the more the Banking Clan can ask. Paying the debt down in the yearly budget, or guaranteeing the Clan's independence, loosens its grip.*

- @deregulate: Lift the rules on the Banking Clan's lending.
- @seat: Give the Clan's friends the Finance chair.
- @refuse: Refuse, and pay the higher rates.

@deregulate
subtitle: The guilds are pleased and San Hill's star rises; corruption grows.
on-arrival: guild_relation += 6; corruption += 2; banking_dereg = 1; debt -= 1; guild_grievance -= 0.1

The Clan's lending rules are relaxed "for the duration". Credits flow, and so does influence.

@seat
subtitle: The Finance & Commerce chair goes to the guilds; the debt is eased a little.
on-arrival: {! if (Q.chair_finance === 'rc') Q.lost_finance = 1; Q.chair_finance = 'guild'; Q.guild_relation += 8; Q.debt -= 2; Q.rimward_dissent += 4; !}

The Finance & Commerce Committee passes to the guilds' nominee. [? if lost_finance : The Caucus loses the chair, and with it the right to write the budget. ?]

@refuse
subtitle: Interest rises for two years; the guilds tighten their embargo.
on-arrival: {! Q.debt_premium_until = Q.date + 24; Q.guild_embargo += 1; Q.guild_relation -= 5; Q.faith += 0.5; SW.guildPatience(Q, -8, 'refusing the Banking Clan'); !}

The Republic will not be lectured by its creditors. San Hill bows, and raises the rate.
